00:36:26,380 --> 00:36:28,640
that we hear a lot of from folks

424
00:36:28,640 --> 00:36:32,000
when they are typing in questions into the chat

425
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:35,060
during Ask TIPA Anything or even our dementia,

426
00:36:35,080 --> 00:36:37,520
problem solvers with the PAC team

427
00:36:37,520 --> 00:36:41,740
is that their mom or dad or loved one

428
00:36:41,740 --> 00:36:44,180
is already in a situation

429
00:36:44,180 --> 00:36:47,180
where they're being taken advantage of

430
00:36:47,180 --> 00:36:49,680
or they're noticing they're being taken advantage of

431
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:53,000
by another sibling or a relative.

432
00:36:54,520 --> 00:36:58,660
And this particular loved one is living with brain change.

433
00:36:58,840 --> 00:37:01,540
And they just are desperate to figure out

434
00:37:01,540 --> 00:37:04,540
what can they do to help protect,

435
00:37:05,080 --> 00:37:07,260
that loved one in that situation.

436
00:37:07,980 --> 00:37:11,060
Because they may be saying something to them about it,

437
00:37:11,440 --> 00:37:13,420
but that loved one is like,

438
00:37:13,480 --> 00:37:15,440
no, no, no, it's okay, it's okay.

439
00:37:15,440 --> 00:37:17,040
But they see what's happening.

440
00:37:17,500 --> 00:37:19,540
So that we see that question a lot.

441
00:37:19,640 --> 00:37:21,580
What can they do in those moments

442
00:37:21,580 --> 00:37:24,220
to help protect them when they can see

443
00:37:24,220 --> 00:37:26,560
that they're being taken advantage of?

444
00:37:27,340 --> 00:37:29,900
I guess what you mean by taken advantage of

445
00:37:29,900 --> 00:37:32,380
is basically financial exploitation

446
00:37:32,380 --> 00:37:34,640
is really what we're talking about.

447
00:37:35,080 --> 00:37:37,440
We do see that.

448
00:37:38,140 --> 00:37:40,560
Sometimes we come in on the backside

449
00:37:40,560 --> 00:37:42,020
where it's already happened

450
00:37:42,020 --> 00:37:44,680
and we're trying to clean up some problems.

451
00:37:45,400 --> 00:37:48,540
It can lead to criminal investigation

452
00:37:48,540 --> 00:37:51,840
depending on to what extent this has occurred.

453
00:37:53,180 --> 00:37:56,000
You can use an irrevocable trust

454
00:37:56,000 --> 00:37:59,740
to help secure assets

455
00:37:59,740 --> 00:38:03,120
because then it's the trustee of the trust

456
00:38:03,120 --> 00:38:05,020
that's actually managing the financial situation.

457
00:38:05,020 --> 00:38:05,060
So that's a good thing.

458
00:38:05,060 --> 00:38:07,760
And we're not talking about the person

459
00:38:07,760 --> 00:38:09,760
with brain change being the trustee

460
00:38:09,760 --> 00:38:12,500
and we're not talking about the child

461
00:38:12,500 --> 00:38:18,540
with the proclivity for exploitation, right?

462
00:38:18,620 --> 00:38:20,980
So we're talking about one of the good kids

463
00:38:20,980 --> 00:38:23,140
is going to be the trustee here.

464
00:38:23,520 --> 00:38:26,060
And we're buttoning up the assets

465
00:38:26,660 --> 00:38:31,480
for our vulnerable loved one

466
00:38:31,480 --> 00:38:33,920
and keeping that away from

467
00:38:35,060 --> 00:38:36,680
the child.

468
00:38:36,680 --> 00:38:38,980
So it's really important to keep that in mind

469
00:38:38,980 --> 00:38:40,960
because it can be very difficult

470
00:38:40,960 --> 00:38:43,160
because you may have a habit

471
00:38:43,160 --> 00:38:47,160
or a lifelong habit of supporting a child

472
00:38:47,160 --> 00:38:51,120
and now mom or dad or grandparent or whomever

473
00:38:51,120 --> 00:38:56,120
no longer can afford to support that other child

474
00:38:56,120 --> 00:38:58,180
in the manner that they have grown accustomed

475
00:38:58,180 --> 00:38:59,520
to being supportive

476
00:38:59,520 --> 00:39:02,100
and we're having to cut them off.

477
00:39:02,100 --> 00:39:04,460
Very delicate situation.

478
00:39:05,060 --> 00:39:08,840
Ultimately, you may find yourself in a conservatorship

479
00:39:08,840 --> 00:39:11,740
because a trust can be protective.

480
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:17,600
However, I am totally not an advocate of conservatorships.

481
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:23,100
I believe in trying to stay out of court as much as possible

482
00:39:23,100 --> 00:39:28,100
but a conservatorship will bring court supervision of assets

483
00:39:29,460 --> 00:39:33,740
and a court will look very dimly upon the assets

484
00:39:33,740 --> 00:39:34,680
of a vulnerable older adult.

485
00:39:34,680 --> 00:39:36,680
So I think that's a really important point

486
00:39:36,680 --> 00:39:38,680
that we need to be thinking about

487
00:39:38,680 --> 00:39:40,680
and I think that's what we need to be thinking about

488
00:39:40,680 --> 00:39:42,680
as we're looking at this.

489
00:39:42,680 --> 00:39:44,680
And I think that's the key to the conversation

490
00:39:44,680 --> 00:39:46,680
and I think that's what we need to be thinking about

491
00:39:46,680 --> 00:39:48,680
is how do we make sure that we're not

492
00:39:48,680 --> 00:39:50,680
making the case that we're not supporting

